INTRO = """
<p>The <strong>rk project</strong> is an unattended, months-long search for explicit
Runge&ndash;Kutta tableaus that minimise <em>end-to-end error in Q15 fixed-point arithmetic at a
fixed cycle budget on Cortex-M0+</em> &mdash; instead of the textbook criterion, truncation error
in exact real arithmetic.</p>

<p>The falsifiable claim: classical tableaus were derived assuming exact arithmetic. On an
FPU-less microcontroller in Q15, at step sizes a real controller would use, roundoff dominates
truncation &mdash; so the classically optimal coefficients are not the practically optimal ones,
and nobody has searched the gap between. Prior work (RKTK and its line) searches tableaus
numerically for order and error constants; it does not price coefficients against a hardware
cost model, and it does not evaluate in fixed point. That narrow gap is the project.</p>

<p>Three repositories with three trust levels do the work: <code>rk-harness</code> holds the
verifier, evaluator and cost models and is mounted <em>read-only</em> into the run container;
<code>rk-work</code> accumulates the append-only archive of every verified tableau;
<code>rk-findings</code> receives an auto-generated site of numbers each cycle. This site,
<code>rk-overview</code>, is the human layer on top.</p>
"""

